issue_comments.body:
@wicknicks suggested "unset" would be a better name for the reset operation, as it's more correct. 

We are "resetting" the logger to the root log level, but in reality we are unsetting it's log level so it naturally uses the loggers higher up in the hierarchy

@gwenshap I think I'll change the 10 or so occurrences in the code where we mention reset to unset. sound good?

@wicknicks thanks for the input.

With regards to returning the effective log level, it should always return the ROOT logger's level with our default log4j settings, correct?
I think it makes total sense to use that rather than return the root logger's level

